# Chapter 3 Alds Star

# Overview

Small village on the Southern Coast of Doaden. 
 
Population: 78.  54 live around the main house, the rest in smaller dwellings within a mile. 
 
All the land is owned by Ald.  Everybody works for him in some sense. 
 
The Village supports itself via agriculture.  There are fields and orchards surrounding.  Each family has a private garden.  Most of the fields are Rye and Wheat.  There is also an apple orchard.  One field is dedicated to goats with several dozen. 
 
Most of the crops are used to support with village.  The remaining is sold with the bulk of that going to St. Pyotr's. 
 
Ald's is a late middle aged man.  Bit on the fat side.  Friendly.  Lives a lavish lifestyle by small village standards.  Nice clothing and home.  Good food a ale. 
 
Ald's family consist of three adult children: Agnes (age 24), Thomas (age 19), Bartholomew (age 27).   
Bart serves as the peacekeeper and protector.  He takes his job seriously and makes an effort to act fairly.  He is respected. 
Agnes does little.  Ald dreams of marrying her off to a family of means and station, but she is well past prime and options are limited.  She spends her day in boredom. 
Thomas is a bit lost.  There is no responsibility left for him and no clear future.  Bart is clearly the next generation of leadership for the Village.  Not a bad kid, but wants to leave the village and find a future.  This has led him to have a grumpy attitude in general.  He tends to act rashly. 
 
The villagers don't have much, but live a good life.  The fields produce enough food.  Ald provides homes in exchange for their labor.  There is some money shared when excess supplies are sold.  Ald keeps 75%, so the families never get enough to amass wealth or have any chance of leaving. 
 
Basically, they are given just enough to be content and have a better life than most. 
 
Other villagers: 
William: age 31.  Caretaker of the horses, oxen, and sheep.  His two sons Hugh and Robert help.   
Alice: age 47.  House keeper and cook for Ald.  Tall and skinny with wrinkled and weathered skin.  Before working in Ald's house, she worked the fields until her husband was killed in an accident. 
Walter: age 24.  Works the fields.  Simple man.  Plain spoken.  Polite, but generally uninterested in anything outside his work and family. 
Edith: age 23.  Married to Walter.  Keeps the house.  Like everybody in the village, she works the fields during harvest.  Friendly.  Get excited to meet visitors. 
Matilda: age 7.  Child of Walter and Edith.  Happy child.  Talks a lot. 
Walter: age 22.  Retarded. 
Cecilia: age 51.  Mother of Walter.  She does laundry for much of the Village and cares for Walter.  Widow. 
Joan: age 24.  Daughter of Cecilia.  Works the fields. 
Gilbert: age 23.  Son of Cecilia. 
 
There is no Inn.  Visitors are sent their way once their business is complete unless there is a good reason to invite them to spend the night.  Nothing nefarious, just not the business they are in. 
 
There is no official church presence, but the Villagers believe in the divinity of the Emperor.  Once a week in the evening there is a short small service that most attend.  During holidays Ald hold feasts to celebrate. 
 
It is mid-August.  Harvest starts in a few weeks.  This is an optimistic time when the crops look healthy.  This batch of crops promised a normal yield until recently.  The fields on the north side of the village show signs of disease.  Crops are not a total loss, but the disease is spreading fast.  If those fields are lost, the village will survive, but food will be rationed and there will be nothing left to sell. 
 
Nothing left to sell is not a problem this year since St. Pyotr's stopped buying anything a couple months ago.  They use to buy a couple goats each month and a portion of the excess grain and apples.  Ald has tried to talk to them, but he gets stonewalled and have not been able to speak with anybody in charge. 
 
There is also a predator that has the village uneasy.  Walter found a deer torn apart when he was out hunting.  Parly eaten, but its body was mauled well beyond anything he had ever seen.  He saw tracks that looked like they could have come from a wolf but the claws were more prominent.  In the past week, a couple sheep were also killed by what is assumed to be the same predator. 
 
Bart has been keeping watch the past two days, but seen nothing. 
 
Walter says he saw a monster metal doggy.  He is scared.  Does not want to talk about it and will not leave his house. 
 
There is a pair of cage hounds hunting in the area.  They have strayed far from St. Pyotr.   

# Story (Session Notes)
The sun is on its way down.  Maybe another hour before dusk then another hour of twilight before the only natural source of light will be the moon and stars.  The adventurers are tired to the point of exhaustion.  As the last drops of adrenalin leave their system it is all they can do to stay on their feet. 
 
The receding outline of the ship used for escape by the cultists is still visible asas it sails away with the barrels of blood.  Beyond that, you can see the faint shadows of a mountain range on the mainland.  The shoreline can't be seen, so you estimate a little over 3 miles of dangerous ocean water separate you mainland. 
 
The small group realizes they have no chance to catch up with the ship in a row boat.  Maybe they can take it to the mainland, but not in their current state and not in the dark. 
 
The group decided get some sleep and evaluate things in the morning.  Wolfram suggest the group takes refuge in the crypt, but the Virgl and Luthien override him.  They have no stomach to sleep inside with the corpses of the cultists you just dispatched.  They are also concerned the guardian statues could come back to life. 
 
Firewood is gathered from the edges of the thick jungle surrounding the beach.  A warm fire, some rations supplemented by the berries provided by Virgl and the team begins to feel safe again.  Sleep quickly follows once JonLief volunteers to take watch for the night as he can stay alert to his surroundings enough while he meditates to get the rest he needs. 
 
The next morning the weather is beautiful.  Clear skies and calm water.  During the long voyage to Dol Island, there was little to do on the boat, and studying the captain's maps gave a little entertainment.  The map found on the dead cultist is recognizable as the coast line opposite Dol Island.  The map has towns marked but unlabeled with the exception of a circled location with the hand written title "St. Pyotr". 
 
The group decided to take to row boat to the main land and see if they can find St. Pyotr's Church.  Maybe this is where the cultists were taking the blood.  The team was sent to investigate, stop whatever was happening, and kill everybody.  Wolfram pointed out that what was happening was a mystery still.  It seems reasonable that they should pursue the only lead you have even if it takes you from the island.  Besides, you have no idea how to get back to Volzruk's camp.  It will take months to walk back. 
 
The trip across the water was uneventful.  Landing on a rocky beach a road can be seen.  The MAP shows St Pyotr's is to the East.  The road seems to be the road on the map that leads right to the church.  Along the way, the road passes through a small village if the map is accurate. 
 
The group decided to follow the road in the assumed direction of St Pyotr.  With few supplied and no coin, there was no other valid options. 
 
After about an hour walk, the group approaches a small village.  There is a person working in a field on the village outskirt.  It is too far to get a clear view, but the person in the field looks to be some type of little person.  When the person sees the ragtag group, they drop their hoe and run towards the village.  You can hear a high pitched male voice shouting "invaders!". 
 
"Secure your weapons.  Try to look friendly." says JonLief.  "We don't need more trouble and these villagers may know something useful about the cultists." 
 
"Or they could be the cultists" replies Virgl. 
 
The group is met at the entrance of the village by an older male halfling.  He is carrying a pitchfork and looks angry. 
 
"I told your people I have not made up my mind yet and needed more time.  That was just three days ago!  Keep pushing me and there is no chance I will ever agree to a deal with the likes of you!" says the little man as he stares at Virgl.  "Now be on your way before I run you off my lands." 
 
At the side of the halfling is another halfling man with bright red hair.  These appear to by typical halfling villages in a typical farming community.  What stands out, other than the anger, is there skin is green.  Not a slight tint but rather unmistakenly green skin.  Halflings are not uncommon.  Everybody in the group what have had many interactions with halflings.  Never has anybody seen nor heard of a green halfling. 
 
"I don't know what you are talking about." exclaims Virgl. 
 
"Three days ago I told that other group from the Alchemical Order the same thing I am telling you know.  I have not decided yet if I am willing to sell three wagons of my cabbages to you!  No go back to your masters and tell them if I see you again before the harvest I will burn the fields before giving you a single leaf." huffs the small man.  "I have a lot of work to do, good day." 
 
"Ah, I see the confusion.  I am no longer part of the Alchemical Order.  Yes, I was once a member, but we, ah, no longer agree on some core principals."  explains Virgl. 
 
"Don't care.  I don't trust you any more than I trusted them.  My Gran Poppy always said you can't trust the Order.  Medeling in things that are not natural and always scheming."  says the little guy.  "Come on Red, lets run 'em off.  We got a posse to organize." 
 
Both raise their pitchfork and start walking forward menacingly.  Wolfram steps in front of them as prongs of their pitchforks nears his thighs. 
 
In the center of the village Wolfram can clearly see a large church.  With his hands raised, Wolfram states "Gentlemen, there is no need for violence.  We are not part of the Alchemical Order and we are not hear to cause you any harm.  We are Penitents of the Church on an important mission.  Our pursuit of some heretics led us here." 
 
Both men take a step back. "Heretics!  We aint no heretics.  We serve the Emperor, may he rise again!" squeaks Red. 
 
"Take it easy Red." says the little man.  He looks back at Wolfram "We got off on the wrong foot.  My name is Ald.  This village is called Ald's Star.  Were an Emperor fearing village and pray for his return.  You will find no better servants to the church on this entire coast!" 
 
"That is good to hear.  We will leave you in peace, but first I request you answer some questions.  As I said, we are pursuing heretics and could use your help."  says Wolfram. 
 
"Of course, of course.  But it needs to be quick, I have a posse to organize." says Ald. 
 
"Little dude, why are you green?" blurts out Luthien. 
 
"Why are you not green" snaps back Ald. 
 
"Sorry little dude, I just never seen a green halfling.  Are you half orc or something?" asks Luthien. 
 
"Half orc! Half orc!  Why I have never been so insulted.  I am one hundred percent halfling.  My poppy was a halfling.  My grand poppy was a halfling.  My family has farmed this land for generations and every one of them halflings." fumes Ald. 
 
He stops and takes a breath.  
 
"But I suppose we are the first green halflings you have ever seen.  We are the only green halflings in the world far as we know.  Not always been this way.  It started during my grand poppy's time.  He cultivated the special cabbages we grow.  The most nutritious and delicious cabbage you have ever eaten.  It is the main thing we eat and is why we are all so healthy and strong.  What's even better is if you eat it every day your eventual turn this beautiful color of green." says Ald with his chest puffed out with pride. 
 
"Fascinating!  What are you doing to make your cabbage so special." asks Virgl as he steps forward in interest. 
 
Ald steps back.  "Nothing really.  We grow them pretty much that same as all the other villages in the area.  Only difference is we only grow from seeds from our own harvest. Our strain of cabbage was developed by my grand poppy." 
 
Wolfram interjects, "Why do you need a posse?" 
 
"Fascinating!  Is your cabbage magical?" Virgil asks. 
 
"Magic? We don't have any magic users in the village.  Hard to trust wizards and the like.  We are simple and honest people.  We grow cabbages the old fashioned way – hard work and love of the land" replies Ald. 
 
Wolfram step up interrupting, "Why do you need a posse? Surly not to kick us out?" 
 
"No, no, the posse is to deal with a wolf.  A rabid wolf we think.  Been attacking our goats and sheep at night the last few weeks" explains Ald. 
 
"Rabid?  That sounds dangerous." replies Wolfram. 
 
"Well, we don't know it is rabid but we do know there is something wrong with that wolf.  It is not simply killing and eating the animals.  It is tearing them apart.  Never seen anything like it.  My boy Bart usually takes cars of predators.  Good boy.  Strong boy raised on health cabbages!  But this feels different.  I don't want him out hunting alone.  Forming a posse and killing the wolf tonight!" boasts Ald. 
 
"How big is this wolf?  Are you sure it is a single wolf?" Queries Wolfram. 
 
"Well, we don't know.  Not seen it.  Just the remains of the livestock it killed.  Could be more than one I suppose, but there are not a lot of tracks so guessing just one lone rabid wolf.  The tracks are pretty big." Says Ald. 
 
"I will offer my services.  As you can see, I am an experienced warrior.  Back in my homeland I frequently hunted monsters that would terrorize our farmsteads.  Of course, as a representative of the Church, I would do this with no expectation of payment."  exclaims Wolfram. 
 
Luthien turns to Wolfram with a startled look.  "Uh, dude, no payment?  You know, like, we have no money.  Not a single copper." 
 
"You are a big one!  I would surely appreciate your help! Can't pay you.  Sorry.  We bring in very little money to the village.  We grow our cabbages and eat most of them.  The only source of income for the village are cabbages and goats we sell to St. Pytor's.  They stopped buying supplies a few months ago.  Not sure how we are going to make end meet now.  Might have to sell cabbages to those slimy Alchemists." Says Ald. 
 
"St Pyotr?  What a fortunate coincidence.  We are on our way to that church.  Any information you can give us about that church would be a great assistance and be full payment for my help slaying your wolf." Says Wolfram 
 
"Church?" Ald chuckles. "That's no church son.  It's a loony bin!" 
 
"Supper is almost ready.  Eat with us while we discuss our wolf problem and I will tell you about St. Pyotr. 
 
The party follows Ald to the dining hall located inside the Church in the middle of the small village.  The room is fill with a couple dozen halflings with light green skin.  Some are talking about the day work in the fields, some are bustling about getting the nightly supper ready.  Everybody freezes when the party enters with Ald. 
 
"This is Wolfram, Jon Leif, Luthien, and, uh, Virgil.  They are Penitents from the Church passing through.  They have important business for the Church.  They will dine with us ang get some much needed rest.  In addition, they have arrived at our time of need.  This big guy is going to help us with the wolf.  The Emperor provided.  May he rise again!" Says Ald to the entire room. 
 
"May he rise again" responds the halflings out of ingrained habit. 
 
Slowly the halflings get back to their conversations and work. 
 
"I don't trust them" says Virgil. 
 
"I sense they are a good people.  You are still bristling over the misunderstand about the Alchemical Order." Says Wolfram. 
 
"We will see.  I am going to investigate.  Get there attention while sneak out.  I will transform into a spider and fine out what they are hiding." 
 
"I want nothing to do this with this" says Wolfram as he walks off. 
 
"I agree" says Jon Lief.  He turns to follow Wolfram. 
 
"Mushroom dude, I'll help.  Been a while since I had an audience!"  says Virgil.  He unslings his guitar and starts tuning it. 
 
Luthien walks to the front of the room and without a word start to play.  The halflings have never heard music of this quality.  Virgil's playing is lively yet precise.  His voice carries throughout the hall filled with mirth.  He captures the attention of the halflings immediately. 
 
Virgil used this opportunity to slip out and turns into a spider. 
 
Luthien's first song is a tradition folk song about the satisfaction one gets from a successful harvest.  The halflings can deeply relate and erupt in cheers when the song ends.  Elated by the crowds response, Luthien rolls into a song of his own composition.  A fast paced song that was a big hit in the taverns. 
 
The song is titled "The Nuns of Nantucket".  The tune is catchy, but it does not take long for the halflings to catch onto the lyrics.  This song very well could be used to define the word sacrilegious. 
 
Ald quickly rushes to Luthien's side, grabs his arm, and starts pulling him to the side while loudly exclaiming "Thank you Luthien.  Wonderful performance, just wonderful.  Please give him a round of applause.  Dinner is ready!" 
 
"We are an Emperor fearing village!  I have never heard something so disrespectful.  How can you possibly be a representative of the Church!" Demands Ald. 
 
"I don't represent the Church little dude.  I serve the Church, but not by choice.  The Church has never done anything for me but cause pain." Spans back Luthien.  His usually happy go lucky demenor replaced by anger. 
 
Jon Lief steps in "So sorry Ald.  Luthinen is a renowned musician.  Very popular in the big cities where piety is not valued as highly as it is here.  You have my apologies." 
 
"Backwards pumpkin bumpkins.  I should wrap my guitar around your..." Luthien grumbles as Jon Lief ushers him off. 
 
Meanwhile, Virgil has returned and is no longer a spider.  His search turned up nothing.  The village seems to be a simple farming village. 
 
Supper is cabbage with a little spiced goat.  Everybody except Virgil eats the food.  It is shockingly good in a comfort food soft of way.  It is easy to see how a meal like this would fortify one for a days work in the fields. 
 
After supper when the sun has gone down the party gathers and prepares to go to the fields where the wolf was last seen. 
 
"I want to thank you again for helping us.  Something seems wrong about this wolf.  The posse will be the four of you plus Red, my son Bart, and me" explains Ald. 
 
"It absolutely will not.  I am coming too.  There will be no discussion or another word said on the matter" boldly states a small halfling woman of middle age.  The glare on her face makes it clear any objections will be fruitless. 
 
The party travels to the grazing field where sheep were last slaughtered by the wolf and settles in to watch.  An hour goes by in silence and then a deep growling is heard in the distance.  The party springs to their feet alert and ready with weapons in hand. 
 
A great beast on four legs come bounding out of the darkness.  It has the features of a wolf but is a bit larger than the largest wolf anyone has even seen.  But what stands out is the beast appears mutilated.  Flaps of skin hand from its body.  Blood seeps from open cuts.  Around the head and body are iron bars.  The bars are visible in places and go into the body in others.  A few iron spikes jut out of the body and appear to be attached to the bars. 
 
Before anybody can react, the beast leaps at Alice.  Its front paws hit her in the chest driving her to the ground.  Its jaws clamp around her throat tearing it out so violently her head is separated from her body. 
 
The party closes in on the beast.  It is too late to save Alice, but this creature must be stopped before more harm can be done.  Bart and Wolfram close it and begin battle. 
 
With the parities attention on the attack on Alice, the second, unseen, beast take the opportunity to come in from behind.  It charges at Red and sinks its teeth into his mid section.  The beast picks Red up in his jaws and violently shakes him until there is spray of blood and entrails.  The beast drops Red to the ground dead and begins creeping toward Jon Lief with a deep gurgling growl. 
 
Th battle with the first beast goes back and forth.  The iron bars block more damage than one would expect.  Finally Wolfram's sword find purchase in an unprotected area just above the monsters shoulders.  His sword comes crashing down not stopping until it reaches the earth leaving the beast in two pieces. 
 
The second beast engages with Virgil and Luthien.  Luthien's rapier proves to have little effect, but he casts a spell that temporarily immobilizes the creature while Virgil dispatches it with a blow from his staff empowered by exploding fungus. 
 
The party carries the remain of Alice and Red back to the Church.  Virgil drags the corpse of one of the beasts with him. 
 
Tears run down Ald's face.  "Red and Alice were good halflings.  Salt of the earth and lovers of the Emperor.  What were those things?  Will there be more?" 
 
Wolfram speaks calmly and reassuringly.  "I could sense they were not from this realm.  The came from outside this world.  I don't know if they will be back, but I am positive there are no more in your immediate area.  Now that I have encountered them, my senses are attuned to the them and I would feel their evil presence from even a couple miles away.  However, be safe.  Don't go out after dark for a while.  Don't travel alone." 
 
"Alone or in a group, my people stand no chance against a monster like that.  Had you and your friends not been with us tonight we would have all died." Says Ald. 
 
Virgil approaches, gore still sticking to his hands.  "I just examined the corpse I brought back.  I can confirm it is not of this world.  The physiology is unlike anything I have ever seen or read about.  I put the remains in the firepit out back." 
 
"Thank you.  Its late and tomorrow is a long day.  I have to tell the village what happened tonight and begin the ceremonies for the dead.  Please stay in Red house tonight.  If you are hungry, there will be food stores in his pantry." Says Ald. 
 
The party goes to Red's house.  It is discomforting to be in the home of a man you just saw torn apart by a monster just a couple of hours ago.  You find sealed jars of pickled cabbage in the kitchen.  Nobody is hungry, but you decide to take the six jars.  After all, you have no money and little supplies. 
 
The party beds down for the might. 